/E (He also mentions this e-wallet service during his interview with Wagner. The latter allegedly lost 25 000 bitcoins when this service was taken down, which he mentions in a video released shortly after the incident. Wagner advocates against reversing the transactions, emphasizes the importance of not leaving funds in in service providers or exchanges, expresses regret for having promoted mybitcoin.com to his friends and family, and reiterates that bitcoin was not hacked but a trusted intermediary went AWOL with people's coins. To my knowledge, there is no record as to whether PLATO lost funds on mybitcoin.com, which happened 27 July that year, at which time when he was nearing the end of his journey.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [38 430 0 R 40]
>>
